# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Source workbooks
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# MDT's three published spreadsheets, ~150 MB, fetched by `npm run data` from
# mdt.mt.gov. Not redistributed here: they are a third party's dataset, they
# are revised in place without a version string, and a copy committed today is
# a copy that quietly disagrees with the source in six months. data/.cache.json
# records the ETag and mtime of what was fetched, so the next run knows whether
# anything changed.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, "data/" matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth -- which silently swallowed site/public/data, the one
# generated directory this repo deliberately tracks.
/data/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Build output
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
node_modules/
site/dist/
site/.astro/

# Screenshots the browser suites write on every run.
site/test-output/
test-output/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Generated from crashmap.config.json -- do not edit, do not commit
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The identity palette, derived and contrast-checked by
# site/scripts/build-theme.mjs. Committing it would let an edited copy outlive
# the config it came from, which is the one thing the generator exists to
# prevent. `npm run build` regenerates it.
site/src/styles/theme.css

# The Content Security Policy, written by site/scripts/build-headers.mjs from
# the basemaps the config names. Same reason: a committed copy is one that
# still permits the previous basemap's origins and not the current one's.
site/public/_headers

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Editors / OS
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
.env

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# What is deliberately NOT ignored
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# site/public/data/ -- the built bundle, ~700 KB, IS committed.
#
# It is generated output, which normally argues for ignoring it. Three things
# argue louder the other way:
#
#   - Cloning and running it has to work. Rebuilding the bundle means a 150 MB
#     download from MDT and several minutes of parsing; a reader who wants to
#     see whether this is worth their time should not have to spend that first.
#   - CI has to be able to run without reaching mdt.mt.gov at all. A test suite
#     that fails when someone else's web server is down is a test suite people
#     learn to ignore.
#   - It is the fixture the decode suite checks the pipeline against. The whole
#     point of that suite is that the committed bundle and freshly built one
#     agree; it needs both.
#
# The tradeoff is that the committed bundle is one county's, built on one date.
# meta.json records which, and when, and from what.
